# Chess960 perft suite — fast tier, all 960 starting positions at depths 1-3.
#
# Format: <FEN> ;D<depth> <nodes> ...   '#' and blank lines ignored.
#
# Castling rights use Shredder-FEN: the FILE LETTER of each castling rook,
# uppercase for White, lowercase for Black, kingside rook first. The standard
# chess start position therefore appears here as "HAha", not "KQkq". Your parser
# must accept both this and X-FEN's KQkq form, and must round-trip whichever it
# was given -- that is the stage 1 gate.
#
# PROVENANCE. These positions were enumerated exhaustively, not copied: all
# arrangements of RNBQKBNR with bishops on opposite colours and the king between
# the rooks. That is exactly 960, which is the first check that the enumeration
# is right. Counts were generated with Stockfish 18 in UCI_Chess960 mode, which
# was first confirmed to reproduce the standard Kiwipete count. The generator
# itself is validated by the standard chess start position, which is one of the
# 960 and must give 20 / 400 / 8902 -- if the FEN construction or the castling
# field were wrong, that line would disagree.
#
# WHY ALL 960 AND NOT A SAMPLE. Castling is the only rule that differs in
# Chess960, and the interesting cases are structural: king already on its
# destination square, rook already on its destination square, king and rook
# adjacent, castling across squares occupied by other back-rank pieces. A sample
# chosen by hand tests the cases you thought of. The full set tests the ones you
# did not -- which is the entire reason this file exists.
#
# Total: 8,224,968 nodes. Fast enough for a debug build. Depths 4-5 are in
# perft-chess960-deep.epd.

